    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21493" root="شأف" body-key="$">
    
      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَائِمْ بِأَصْحَابِكَ</span></b>  <i>Take thou the direction of
the left hand with thy companions:</i> (S, K, TA:)
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَامِنْ</span> signifies “ take thou the direction of the
right hand. ” (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَآمَ</span> <i>He</i> (a man)
<i>came to</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الشَّأْم</span> [i. e. <i>Syria</i>]: like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَامَنَ</span> signifying
“ he came to El-Yemen. ” (TA. [See also 4.])

